1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,085
A two-inch, stem-mounted magnetron.

2
00:00:03,085 --> 00:00:06,700
The NW100 plate is the chamber interface.

3
00:00:06,700 --> 00:00:11,019
The feedthrough and coolant fittings are outside.

4
00:00:11,019 --> 00:00:14,017
The target faces into the chamber.

5
00:00:14,267 --> 00:00:18,679
The KF25 clamp grips the feedthrough and mating stub.

6
00:00:18,679 --> 00:00:22,425
The metal centering ring locates the flanges.

7
00:00:22,425 --> 00:00:25,505
Its O-ring seals between their faces.

8
00:00:25,505 --> 00:00:30,750
The stub, NW100 plate, and hollow stem form the grounded mount.

9
00:00:31,000 --> 00:00:38,557
DC or the output of a 13.56 megahertz matching network drives the same center conductor, one at a time.

10
00:00:38,557 --> 00:00:41,638
A socket joins the copper tube to the rod.

11
00:00:41,638 --> 00:00:44,132
The ceramic guide centers the rod.

12
00:00:44,132 --> 00:00:49,048
The ceramic carrier separates the grounded stem from the live head.

13
00:00:49,048 --> 00:00:54,550
The external terminal enclosure and carrier retention still need detailing.

14
00:00:54,800 --> 00:00:57,726
Each line begins at an external bulkhead.

15
00:00:57,726 --> 00:01:05,364
Inside the stem, an angled transition leads to a dielectric section, then a metal tube at the powered head.

16
00:01:05,364 --> 00:01:08,861
The dielectric sections interrupt the metal path.

17
00:01:08,861 --> 00:01:11,502
The coolant itself can still conduct.

18
00:01:11,502 --> 00:01:17,283
Both lines pass through the carrier, locator, and yoke into the copper backplate.

19
00:01:17,533 --> 00:01:21,199
Eight outer magnets surround an annular center magnet.

20
00:01:21,199 --> 00:01:24,660
All nine are five millimeters thick in this layout.

21
00:01:24,660 --> 00:01:30,837
They sit flush in a separate nonmagnetic locator and touch the rear face of the steel yoke.

22
00:01:30,837 --> 00:01:34,977
The copper head seats directly against the front of the yoke.

23
00:01:34,977 --> 00:01:37,217
The yoke is at cathode potential.

24
00:01:37,467 --> 00:01:42,921
The backplate, C-channel core, and target-seat cover are separate copper pieces.

25
00:01:42,921 --> 00:01:47,011
Three head screws pass through dry zones around the channel.

26
00:01:47,011 --> 00:01:52,534
The divider lies between inlet and outlet so water must sweep around the channel.

27
00:01:52,534 --> 00:01:56,283
The closure and tube seals are still open design items.

28
00:01:56,533 --> 00:01:59,195
Blue shows the proposed supply path.

29
00:01:59,195 --> 00:02:07,773
Water enters the backplate, travels around the C-shaped channel behind the target, and exits into the orange return.

30
00:02:07,773 --> 00:02:11,174
Heat crosses the target seat into the coolant.

31
00:02:11,174 --> 00:02:13,688
The moving markers show direction.

32
00:02:13,688 --> 00:02:16,350
They do not represent measured flow.

33
00:02:16,600 --> 00:02:22,263
The 50.8 millimeter aluminum target seats flat against the copper cover.

34
00:02:22,263 --> 00:02:29,263
The ring has a 48 millimeter opening and overlaps the target by 1.4 millimeters per side.

35
00:02:29,263 --> 00:02:34,689
Three recessed screws, 120 degrees apart, clamp the ring to the seat.

36
00:02:34,689 --> 00:02:38,150
Screw threads and preload are not validated.

37
00:02:38,400 --> 00:02:41,487
The shield bolts to its grounded rear seat.

38
00:02:41,487 --> 00:02:47,877
The 72.8 millimeter side bore leaves a two millimeter radial gap around the powered head.

39
00:02:47,877 --> 00:02:50,175
The inward lip covers the clamp.

40
00:02:50,175 --> 00:02:56,063
The shield comes off toward the chamber interior before the target can be removed.

41
00:02:56,063 --> 00:03:01,017
Its 92 millimeter mounting flange must clear the actual chamber port.

42
00:03:01,267 --> 00:03:06,959
This is the native SolidWorks R06 geometry, with all 45 part instances.

43
00:03:06,959 --> 00:03:12,171
The four reported overlaps are at the angled coolant transitions.

44
00:03:12,171 --> 00:03:20,188
Before fabrication, resolve those joints, the carrier retention, and the enclosed power termination.

45
00:03:20,188 --> 00:03:27,083
Verify seals, cooling, the magnetic field, and electrical clearance in both DC and RF.
